L.append('| Item | Convention |')
L.append('|---|---|')
L.append('| Units / axes | Metres, Y up, front faces **+Z**. Import with **Scale Factor 1**, Convert Units off. Unity\'s OBJ importer handles the handedness flip. |')
L.append('| Pivots | `floor`: lowest point at y = 0, centred in x/z. `wall`: back face at z = 0, centred in x and y, facing +Z (put the pivot on the wall). `ceiling`: top at y = 0, hanging down (put the pivot on the ceiling). `none`: see the model row (CCTVDome and RecessedDownlight: y = 0 is the ceiling surface; door handles: origin on the door face). |')
L.append('| `<Name>.obj/.mtl` | One OBJ group and material per surface. `map_Kd` points at the colour map; the Normal and MetallicSmoothness file names are written as `# Normal ...` / `# MetallicSmoothness ...` comment lines in the MTL and listed in models.json. Unity reads only Kd, `map_Kd` and `d`, so assign the other maps in code (DemoAssetLibrary) or on the material. OBJ files carry welded `v/vt/vn` (authored normals). |')
L.append('| `_Color.jpg/.png` | Base colour, sRGB. |')
L.append('| `_Normal.jpg` | Tangent-space normal map, OpenGL +Y (= Unity). Texture Type **Normal map**, strength 1. |')
L.append('| `_MetallicSmoothness.png` | R = G = B = metallic, A = smoothness. **sRGB off**. Standard: Metallic slot, Source = Metallic Alpha, Smoothness scale 1 (same as ForensicModels, PBRExterior, NightMaterials). |')
L.append('| Constant materials | No maps: use Kd plus the `metallic` / `smoothness` values in models.json (e.g. Chrome 1 / 0.92, Aluminium 1 / 0.7, Rubber 0 / 0.25). |')
L.append('| Glass | MTL `d` < 1 (frame glass 0.12, clock 0.18, pendant shade 0.25, dome 0.55, water bottle 0.35). Use the project glass material (Standard Fade/Transparent, smoothness ~0.95). |')
L.append('| Emission | models.json marks emissive surfaces (`emission`): monitor screens, ExitSign face, TrackLight/RecessedDownlight lenses, LEDPanel diffuser, pendant and desk-lamp bulbs, CCTV IR LEDs, smoke-detector LED. Use the Color map (or a warm/cool white) as emission when lit. |')
L.append('| Shared_* textures | Seamless 512 px tiling materials used by the project-made models (PlasticBlack, PlasticWhite, FabricCharcoal, MeshWeave, BrushedSteel, PowderCoatGrey). Those models have world-scale UVs; keep Wrap Mode = Repeat. |')
L.append('| Two-sided parts | Unity\'s Standard shader culls back faces, so every thin part carries explicit back faces (a reversed copy with negated normals): SnakePlant leaves, the office-chair mesh back, the PottedPlantTall leaf cards and the PottedPlantArrowhead leaves. The other models need no back faces from normal viewpoints (checked in software renders with back-face culling). No double-sided shader needed. |')
